However, deploying LLMs on resource-constrained edge devices presents significant challenges.

Firstly,  the computational and memory constraints impose substantial limitations on LLM loading and inference. LLMs often consist of billions of parameters, resulting in massive memory footprints that exceed the RAM capacities of most edge devices (Chen et al., 
2023c
). For example, a LLaMA-2 (Touvron et al., 
2023b
) model with 7B parameters requires over 8GB of memory even in FP16 precision. Without compression techniques, edge devices risk latency spikes and memory overflow during model loading (Lin et al., 
2024
