34:6062–9.")]. Meta-learning approaches, such as MAML, demonstrate effectiveness in adapting to new tasks through gradient-based optimization. In contrast, Prototypical Networks excel in few-shot image classification tasks by creating a metric space where prototypes of each class are calculated. Utilizing pre-trained language models for transfer learning emphasizes the robustness of contextual embedding in zero-shot scenarios, enabling models to understand subtle language patterns with minimal task-specific training [
